<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ica3aba358d141a7df9a3e97251d4c1e520cbf2c8" commit="0dd83a1cd168caff8fc8cc459fd4d8efed1a932e" commit_message="driver: Move sensor private struture definition to boards.  sensor private structure for bmi160 and bmp280 were defined in the drivers themselves. It worked because there was only one instance of each sensors on a board. However, this is an error it should be in board files, as it was done for other sensors like the kionix.  BUG=none TEST=buildall. BRANCH=kevin,reef  Change-Id: Ica3aba358d141a7df9a3e97251d4c1e520cbf2c8 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424218 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424218" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/18/424218/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I40fbe3040c98c2698221b52aaadaf5519da13312" commit="30ed2bd3f933ffdb7921ef58bf9b4f45b69ce72f" commit_message="common: Add BOARD variable when listing the tasks.  Some board (kevin), use BOARD_KEVIN variable to specify the task list. We need this variable to be provided to CPP when generating _tsk_lst.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59423 TEST=Check with echo &quot;CONFIG_TASK_LIST&quot; | arm-none-eabi-cpp -P -Iboard/kevin \ -D&quot;TASK_NOTEST(n, r, d, s)=n&quot; -D&quot;TASK_ALWAYS(n, r, d, s)=n&quot; \ -DBOARD_KEVIN=y -imacros ec.tasklist That the proper task list is generated. BRANCH=kevin,reef  Change-Id: I40fbe3040c98c2698221b52aaadaf5519da13312 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424219 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424219" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_co