rt a light/proximity sensors are a cros_ec sensor, with this module, we can report the sensor to ARC++  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59423 TEST=On reef with special firmware, check the module is loaded.  Change-Id: Id23170297c707c833deccf15ed44993d0e7e9e3e Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424217 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424217" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/17/424217/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I42c0007ca012ca46ee6cbba80ac94a2570b8d262" commit="5c07ec860a473a51554efbcadf77b3ebb7b5aa7e" commit_message="Deprecate venv_command  BUG=chromium:674687 TEST=Run virtualenvs locally  Change-Id: I42c0007ca012ca46ee6cbba80ac94a2570b8d262 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423334 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423334" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/infra_virtualenv" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/infra_virtualenv" ref="refs/changes/34/423334/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifb52fadf53e6bf40883fe5ab30fe1615e28cfbc7" commit="4f4a9fddc1a88bd76c402a5633bf7fe4faed6958" commit_message="samus-pre-flight-branch: disable hugepage when profiling  AutoFDO doesn't work well with perf.data collected on hugepage enabled processes.  BUG=chromium:641088 TEST=chromeos_config_unittest  Change-Id: Ifb52fadf53e6bf40883fe5ab30fe1615e28cfbc7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424189 Commit-Ready: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting-Yuan Huang &lt;laszio@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424189" owner_email="laszio@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/89/424189/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If54077acf1ca164473d767ae839b885ecedabfee" commit="b40804b8398c7733518665f5a73d6320778804cb" commit_message="shill: use base::MakeUnique&lt;T&gt; when possible  This CL replaces      std::unique_ptr&lt;T&gt; x(new T(...));  and other similar variants with      auto x = base::MakeUnique&lt;T&gt;(...);  as the latter is preferred over the former by not referring to T twice, which makes the code more concise while preserving its readability.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: If54077acf1ca164473d767ae839b885ecedabfee Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424313 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424313" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/13/424313/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I740529a7957e43bc23dfc494d94a3ad6ec47c072" commit="cb5adfdccbb6c4e9b11f3a06d0b4f1b92ca904dc" commit_message="media-rules: Add udev trigger for mtk-jpeg  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43703 TEST=Boot my elm and make sure /dev/jpeg-dec is created as a symlink to      the mtk-jpeg device.  Change-Id: I740529a7957e43bc23dfc494d94a3ad6ec47c072 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415648 Commit-Ready: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="415648" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/48/415648/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1fdba0512ac5a85b113a8284216c8b00f1564a94" commit="8881815920ad53d58e7024726089b94f4652b1d6" commit_message="fix memory size calculations in host/test mode  The common/system.c:system_usable_ram_end() function is used to determine how much room there is available for shared memory. This assumes that the jdata container is located at the top of SRAM right below the panic data buffer.  This correct for embedded mode, but when building for host, panic structure is allocated in a different memory block, not necessarily adjacent to the __shared_mem_buf array. This leads to incorrect calculations of the available shared memory amount.  Let's make sure the two memory blocks are adjacent, this way the available memory calculations are accurate.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=verified that      make runtests -j    succeeds, including the new test for malloc/free from shared memory   (coming up in the next patch).  Change-Id: I1fdba0512ac5a85b113a8284216c8b00f1564a94 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424176 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424176" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/76/424176/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icb26043e1ce3145a9d9d5ad159dc709e6b8bf98d" commit="01a02756b4f05be2f80cfcff677695f84be2e5e3" commit_message="Revert &quot;servo_v4: Added initial USB PD support for both CHG/DUT ports&quot;  This reverts commit 167f7e51d8e7693a277077d6c24294d2997e1c55. This CL followed https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/422450/ which needs to be reverted because PSTATE is required for keeping serial numbers.  Change-Id: Icb26043e1ce3145a9d9d5ad159dc709e6b8bf98d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422480 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422480" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/80/422480/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9130.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>